-- paperclip:migration-safety-ignore large-create-index-not-concurrently: The migration runner wraps each migration in a transaction, so CONCURRENTLY is unavailable. Operators already built this index CONCURRENTLY under the same name on running instances, so IF NOT EXISTS makes this a no-op there. Elsewhere it is additive: building it scans issues once and blocks writes to that table for the scan. Two full (company, run) indexes over 5,000 issues measured 24.7 ms, and these partial indexes hold only the issues a run holds, so the pause stays far below a request timeout even at ten times that size.
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS "ops_issues_execution_run_id_idx" ON "issues" USING btree ("execution_run_id") WHERE "issues"."execution_run_id" is not null;--> statement-breakpoint
